WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.380
(pensive music)

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:03.210
- [Narrator] This is the Taiwan Strait.

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:05.790
In recent years, China
has sent military aircraft

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:08.280
across the Strait and towards
the island's southwest

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.840
on a near daily basis,

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.180
repeatedly testing
Taiwan's ability to respond

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:14.610
to an invasion along its west coast.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:17.040
But this year, China
began doing something new.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.180
In April and May,

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.030
Chinese aerial drones went
further than ever before,

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:22.680
circling the entire island,

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.380
and fighter jets were detected
on the island's east coast.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.660
Military experts say
Taiwan has always relied

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.660
on its mountainous terrain as
a natural shield in the event

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.990
of an attack, looking to its
east as a safe place to refuel

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:36.870
and re-arm its fighter jets
if the west coast fell.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.550
So China's growing range has led

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.710
to competing ideas amongst
the island's current

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:44.250
and former military leaders
about how Taiwan should respond.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:48.720
- Terrain cannot protect
ourself anymore compared

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.180
to decades ago.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:52.500
- [Narrator] So how
serious are these threats

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:53.940
to Taiwan's east coast

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.176
and does the island need
to change its strategy?

00:00:56.176 --> 00:00:57.720
(weapon booming)

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:01.350
A key part of Taiwan's current
strategy can be found here.

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:03.690
This satellite imagery
shows an air force base

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:06.390
on the island's east
that's over 30 years old.

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:08.850
Bunkers built deep into the
mountains store fighter jets

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.920
and anti-ship missiles like these

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:11.970
that could launch in response

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:15.180
to an attack on the main
infrastructure in Taiwan's west.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:17.250
By sheltering these
weapons in the mountains,

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.200
Taipei plans to be able to prevent China

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.390
from gaining early control of the skies.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:22.680
Experts say this is crucial

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.120
because the People's Liberation Army

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.220
of China dwarfs Taiwan's military,

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:28.140
limiting the island's capacity to defend

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:31.140
against a full-scale invasion
from China on its own.

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:33.480
Instead, its main strategy
has been to survive

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:34.860
in the east until allies,

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:38.160
including the US can arrive
to assist the island.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.260
But some experts say
China's recent incursions

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:43.500
to the island's east and
its growing military prowess

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:46.230
are making Taiwan's
current strategy outdated.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:47.850
- You can see the developments

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:51.360
in the modernization of the PLA.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.250
They have a lot of the measure

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:56.837
and the capability attack
from the eastern side.

00:01:56.837 --> 00:02:00.523
So eastern side is not as safe

00:02:00.523 --> 00:02:05.340
as we thought the decades ago.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.470
- Retired Admiral Lee
Hsi-Min served for more

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:09.900
than 40 years in Taiwan's armed forces,

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:12.930
retiring in 2019 as the
chief of general staff.

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:15.480
Since leaving Taiwan's
military, he's advocated

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.310
for the island to focus on smaller,

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:20.070
widely distributed defenses
rather than attempting

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:22.320
to match China's offensive capabilities.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:26.100
- We have to change the overall thinking

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:29.490
about how to build up our capability.

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:33.450
If China really wants to invade Taiwan,

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:36.870
I believed he should be very confident

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:39.573
for their A2/AD capability.

00:02:39.573 --> 00:02:40.406
(pensive music)

00:02:40.406 --> 00:02:43.350
- [Narrator] A2/AD or
anti-access/area denial

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:44.910
is the ability to control access

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:46.800
to a military operations zone,

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.390
usually using long-range missiles

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:51.780
to threaten any enemy forces
that try to enter an area.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.790
A version of this was seen last year

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:55.440
with Chinese military exercises

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.720
that simulated a blockade of Taiwan.

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:00.390
Live fire drills were
carried out in six zones,

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:02.640
blocking maritime traffic in those areas

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.140
and ballistic missiles were fired

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:06.360
into waters off the island's east coast.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:08.910
Admiral Lee says China would
only attempt an invasion

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.530
of the island if they were confident

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:12.570
that their A2/AD capabilities

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:15.120
would blockade Taiwan's
east robustly enough

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:18.120
to dissuade Taiwan's allies
from coming its assistance.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.820
- No one will give you the guarantee

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:24.690
that they will be here to aid

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:27.630
if there's war across the straits.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:28.680
- [Narrator] So instead of investing

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.090
in large conventional weapons,

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.820
like tanks and war ships,
Lee says Taiwan should focus

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:35.550
on mobile and civilian capabilities,

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:39.270
such as portable anti-ship
and anti-air missiles, drones

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:40.530
and radar systems

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.270
that could make an
invasion too challenging

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:43.770
for China to even attempt.

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:48.770
- I believe that the
asymmetrical warfare is the key

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.880
for the weaker side or
for the smaller one.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:56.490
In the early stage of the Ukraine war,

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:59.250
Russia used a lot of the tanks

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:04.250
or armored vehicle trying
to direct the attack Kyiv

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:08.490
but it failed because Ukraine has a lot

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:12.060
of the small symmetrical arms,

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:15.603
like the Stinger or Javelin or and NLAW.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:18.540
- [Narrator] And while
Taiwan is building its supply

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:19.680
of smaller arms,

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:22.230
experts say it will still
need to rely on the assistance

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:24.420
of its allies who are
increasingly signaling

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:26.160
their willingness to defend the island.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.560
A new US access to joint military bases

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:30.540
in the Philippines could play a key role

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.670
in Taiwan's east coast strategy.

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:34.920
These new bases are
located on the other side

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:37.650
of the Bashi channel, a key
access point for the navies

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.720
of both China and the US,

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:42.150
and an important maritime traffic route.

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:44.280
Some US systems, including HIMARS

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:46.890
could reach the south of Taiwan
if placed on the other side

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:48.960
of the channel, allowing
them to strike back

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.480
against the Chinese
invasion attempt remotely.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:52.980
And while China's movements in the east

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.570
have made some experts concerned

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:56.400
about the island's current strategy,

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:59.160
others say Taiwan already
has the capabilities it needs

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:01.020
to stop China from rounding the island

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:02.557
in the event of an invasion.

00:05:02.557 --> 00:05:03.540
(soldiers shouting)
(weapons booming)

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:08.472
- In peace time, you can
let the PLA warplanes

00:05:08.472 --> 00:05:11.280
or warship to go around Taiwan.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:14.820
However, in wartime,
it's another situation.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:18.210
We have the right to defend ourself.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:19.950
- [Narrator] Dr. Su
Tzu-Yun is the director

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:20.910
at Taiwan's Institute

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:23.280
for National Defense
and Security Research,

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:25.380
a think tank funded by
the island's military.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:26.910
He says watching the war in Ukraine

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:29.460
has made it clear that
Taiwan has some advantages

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:31.486
in the event of an invasion attempt.

00:05:31.486 --> 00:05:35.070
- In the Ukraine, it's a
so-called ground battlefield.

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:38.970
However, in Taiwan's case,
it's a maritime battle.

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:42.780
So Taiwan can use limited resources

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:47.780
to create a so-called denial
zone to blockade PLA's navy

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:56.280
or their air force to
enter east side of Taiwan.

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:58.680
- [Narrator] So to do this,
Taiwan is also investing

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:01.980
in larger defensive systems
like the Patriot, and Phalanx,

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:04.080
a cannon mounted on military vessels used

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:06.090
to stop incoming threats.

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:08.550
Taiwan's Defense Ministry
said in earlier remarks

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:10.830
that it won't entirely
rely on its east coast

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:13.110
to be a safe haven in
the event of a conflict,

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:14.850
saying there will be no clear distinction

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:17.610
between the front lines and
the rear during wartime.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.830
While China continues to
signal its capabilities

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:22.680
to take over Taiwan by force if necessary,

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:25.020
the island is increasingly
using its own war games

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:27.000
and exercises to show Beijing

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.490
and the world that it's
able to defend itself.

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:33.600
- I hope our defense
can tell the China side,

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:36.780
can tell PLA, "Don't invade us.

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:41.780
If you invade, you will
suffer lots of the casualty

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:46.530
and you will not able to
occupy Taiwan physically."

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:49.620
So that they will think twice.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:51.060
- [Narrator] But even
as they debate how best

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:54.480
to repel an assault, the
Taiwanese military circle agree

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:57.480
that the best case scenario
is to avoid any conflict

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:58.555
in the Strait.

00:06:58.555 --> 00:07:03.260
(pensive music)
(Weapons shooting)

